codex
Step 0 supports Track B, not Track A. The paper proves existence for all planar graphs and narrows its new casework to \(\Delta\in\{6,7,8\}\), but it does not establish distributional hardness. On this generated triangular-lattice subclass, the standard square-graph greedy algorithm is explicitly efficient; the meaningful benchmark is the gap between thousands of mechanical graph operations and a short mod-7 invariant route.

I found two audit improvements worth making before the oracle run: make random guessing structure-aware by forcing the obvious seven-vertex square-graph clique to receive distinct colors, and strengthen the “obvious coordinate ansatz” attack from one formula to a portfolio of simple mod-7 and mod-19 formulas.
