    25	Section 1 gives the exact definition and Theorem 1.2 proves the bound for every
    26	simple planar graph.  The start of Section 2 says earlier results cover
    27	`Delta <= 5` and `Delta >= 9`; the paper's new work is therefore the
    28	`Delta in {6,7,8}` regime.  These instances use `Delta=6`, hence 19 colors.
    29	Remark 2.1 supplies the deletion-and-extension principle, Lemma 2.2 bounds a
    30	two-neighborhood, and Sections 2.1--2.3 finish the three remaining degree
    31	cases with reducible configurations and discharging.
    32	
    33	Generation does not solve an emitted graph.  Begin with a connected irregular
    34	induced patch of the triangular lattice.  For its three edge directions
    35	`(1,0)`, `(0,1)`, `(1,-1)`, the value `x+3y mod 7` is nonzero on every one of
    36	the 18 nonzero displacements possible in at most two steps.  It is therefore a
    37	seven-color certificate.  The generator carries it through a random lattice
    38	symmetry, large unimodular shears, vertex relabeling, and edge reordering.
    39	
    40	## Why Track B
    41	
    42	The paper proves existence, not average-case or distributional hardness, so a
    43	Track A claim would be unsupported.  An efficient algorithm is explicitly
    44	disclosed here: construct the square graph and apply first-fit coloring.  A
    45	triangular-lattice vertex has at most 18 vertices within two steps, so 19
    46	colors guarantee success in every public vertex order.  The implementation is
    47	`O(n*Delta^2+n*q)`; on eight hard instances it averaged **8,792 counted
    48	set/color operations and 0.000966 s** (maximum 8,881 operations and 0.000993 s).
    49	
    50	The compact route notices the three opposite edge-displacement pairs, gives a
    51	lattice basis mod-7 increments 1 and 3, and carries the resulting increment
    52	along a spanning tree.  At the hard preset that costs 119 modular updates plus
    53	19 setup/direction checks, **138 exact operations**.  The benchmark asks a
    54	no-tool model to find that compression in a shuffled 120-vertex instance; it
    55	does not pretend graph-square greedy coloring is hard with software.
    56	
    57	## Worked demo
    58	
    59	The complete `demo`, seed 0, is genuinely hand-solvable.  Vertex 6 is adjacent
    60	to the other six and those six form a cycle, so every pair of vertices is at
    61	distance at most two; any seven distinct colors work.
    62	
    63	```text
    64	Distance-two coloring of a planar graph
    65	
   105	|---|---:|---:|---:|---|
   106	| demo | 7 | 0 | 1 | hand example; skipped by hardening |
   107	| easy | 48 | 2 | 1 | first oracle rung |
   108	| medium | 84 | 4 | 2 | local gates pass |
   109	| hard | 120 | 6 | 3 | shipping preset; local gates pass, oracle evidence blocked |
   110	
   111	`escalate()` first raises coordinate camouflage and constraint crowding at a
   112	fixed 120-entry answer.  Only after those axes are exhausted does it lengthen
   113	the patch, up to 240 vertices; a further increase returns `cap_bound` because
   114	the 256-atom answer limit becomes binding.
   115	
   116	## Gate results
   117	
   118	| gate | measured result |
   119	|---|---|
   120	| G1 | 12/12 planted witnesses verify across all presets |
   121	| G2 | 5/5 corruption classes rejected with 5 distinct reasons |
   122	| G3 | prose/fence/JSON round-trip passes, garbage is rejected, answer is JSON-native |
   123	| G4 | 0 hits in 200,000 structure-aware samples; space size `P(19,7)*19^113` |
   124	| G5 | hard density 0/200,000; reference 8,891 operations and 0.001073 s on the reporting seed |
   125	| G6 | five attacks at 0/8 each; reference greedy algorithm 8/8 as expected |
   126	| G7 | 240-vertex instance builds and verifies; search-space bits grow 508 to 1018 |
   127	| G8 | 140/140 invariance checks, 140/140 carried witnesses, 20/20 unrelated keys distinct |
   128	| G9(c) | 360 characters, about 90 tokens, 120 atoms, 138 intended operations |
   129	
   130	## Oracle loop and G9 arms
   131	
   132	The required bare, structural-hint, and placebo harnesses were invoked in
