   170	
   171	After a successful bare oracle run and both G9 reruns, emit from the repository
   172	root with:
   173	
   174	```bash
   175	bash scripts/emit.sh 2403.12302 20 hard
   176	```
   177	
   178	## Caveats
   179	
   180	This generated distribution is easy for any implementation of square-graph
   181	greedy coloring; that is the declared Track B reference route.  It tests
   182	recognition and no-tool execution of a lattice invariant, not the difficult
   183	case analysis in the paper's general planar-graph proof and not average-case
   184	graph-coloring hardness.
   185	
   186	The 0/200,000 guess result is not based on naive independent noise: each sample
   187	already gives seven distinct uniform colors to the smallest-ID degree-6 vertex
   188	and its six neighbors, a clique in the square graph, and samples the remaining
   189	slots uniformly.  It says that guesses from that explicit prior are sparse;
   190	it says nothing about a model prior biased toward lattice formulas.  The panel
   191	checks a degree outlier, edge-only greedy, public-index periodic, a portfolio
   192	of `x`, `y`, `x+y`, and `x-y` modulo both 7 and 19, and 256 random restarts.  It
   193	does not test every affine formula; finding the correct affine invariant is
   194	the intended solution.
   195	
   196	The canonical key is exact for vertex relabeling, edge order/reversal,
   197	translation, unimodular coordinate changes, and their tested compositions,
   198	but it is not a complete graph-isomorphism canonical form for arbitrary
   199	planar graphs.  Most importantly, no four-vendor oracle attempt was scored
   200	because the available OpenRouter credential was exhausted, so the local gates
   201	are trustworthy but the required external hardness claim remains pending.
