codex
Implemented a native **Track B** generator based on the paper’s \(\Delta=6\) distance-two coloring regime ([Theorem 1.2](https://arxiv.org/html/2403.12302v3)).

Files:

- [gen_2403_12302.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2403.12302/gen_2403_12302.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2403.12302/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2403.12302/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2403.12302/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2403.12302/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2403.12302/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

All local gates pass. Highlights include 0/200,000 valid structured guesses, five attacks at 0/8, exact planarity checks, 140/140 canonical-key invariance tests, and public-data reconstruction succeeding on 400/400 audited instances.

The external hardening verdict remains pending: Gemini genuinely failed the easy instance, but the OpenRouter key then hit its total quota and four redraws returned HTTP 403. The harness correctly issued no hardness verdict. A funded key must rerun:

```bash
python3 ../../scripts/harden.py gen_2403_12302.py
```

No `REJECTED.md` was created because this is an infrastructure block, not a G/H/V failure.
